.TH RTW89 8
.SH NAME
rtw89 \- Realtek RTL8852CE WLAN driver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aux/rtw89
[
.B -l
.I loglevel
] [
.B -m
.I memlimit
] [
.B -p
.IB name = value
]... [
.B -g
.BI #G/ n
] [
.B -w
.BI #ω/wlan N
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Rtw89
drives Realtek's RTL8852CE (PCI 10ec:c852, Wi-Fi 6E) as the radio of
a
.IR wlan (3)
interface: Realtek's
.I rtw89
driver, as FreeBSD carries it (under its BSD-3-Clause choice), on
nfront's LinuxKPI, with a small 802.11 layer of its own under it in
place of Linux's mac80211.
The kernel's 802.11 code behind the interface scans, authenticates,
associates and ciphers;
.IR wpa (8)
does WPA.
.PP
The card is a device of
.IR gpu (3)
(plan9.ini's
.BR *userpci=10ec/c852 ),
the interface an
.B ether
of type
.B wlan
(plan9.ini's
.BR ether1=type=wlan ).
.I Rtw89
takes the first Realtek device of
.B #G
(or
.BR -g )
and the first interface of
.B #ω
(or
.BR -w );
it reads the card's address from its efuse and writes it to the
interface's
.BR ctl ,
loads the firmware
.B /lib/firmware/rtw89/rtw8852c_fw-2.bin
(or
.BR -1 ,
or without a number), starts the card and passes the frames between
the interface's
.B data
file and the card: the channel the kernel asks for (2.4 GHz channels
1 to 14, 5 GHz above), and when the kernel has associated with an
access point, the association, so that the card's firmware chooses the
rates for it.
.PP
.B -l
sets the level of the driver's messages (as Linux's printk, default 6;
8 shows rtw89's debug messages),
.B -m
where the frames' memory lies, as FreeBSD's
.B compat.linuxkpi.skb.mem_limit
(0 anywhere, 1 below 4 GB, the default, 2 below 64 GB: the card does
not work reliably with frames above 4 GB, FreeBSD's
.IR rtw89 (4)
says; plan9.ini's
.B *dma32
keeps memory there),
.B -p
one of rtw89's module parameters, such as
.B debug_mask=0x...
(its debug messages)
or
.BR disable_aspm_l1=1 .
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
.EX
aux/rtw89
aux/wpa -s mynet -p /net/ether1
ip/ipconfig ether /net/ether1
.EE
.SH FILES
.TF /lib/firmware/rtw89
.TP
.B /lib/firmware/rtw89
the firmware, from linux-firmware
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/aux/rtw89
.br
.B /sys/src/linux/kpi/linux/mac80211.c
.br
.B /sys/src/linux/kpi/linux/wlan.c
.br
.B /sys/src/linux/freebsd/freebsd/sys/contrib/dev/rtw89
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR wlan (3),
.IR gpu (3),
.IR wpa (8),
.IR plan9.ini (8)
.SH BUGS
Written for nfront.
The kernel's 802.11 code knows 802.11a/b/g only: the access point is
the card's legacy station (no HT, VHT or HE rates, no aggregation, no
power save).
6 GHz channels are not used:
.IR wlan (3)'s
channel numbers do not tell
them from 2.4 GHz ones.
No ciphers in the card: frames go and come as the kernel ciphers them.
Not yet run on the hardware.
